# Performance Guidelines

## Code Splitting

- Use dynamic imports for large components
- Implement proper loading states
- Use React.lazy for route-based splitting
- Split vendor bundles from application code

## Optimization

- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Implement proper key props for lists
- Use useMemo and useCallback appropriately
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Optimize bundle size

## Bundle Optimization

- Monitor bundle size with webpack-bundle-analyzer
- Use Next.js built-in optimizations
- Implement proper tree shaking
- Remove unused dependencies
- Use dynamic imports for heavy libraries

## Core Web Vitals

- Optimize Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) - target < 2.5s
- Minimize First Input Delay (FID) - target < 100ms
- Reduce Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) - target < 0.1
- Optimize First Contentful Paint (FCP) - target < 1.8s

## Image Optimization

- Use Next.js Image component
- Implement proper lazy loading
- Optimize image formats (WebP, AVIF)
- Use appropriate image sizes
- Implement responsive images

## Font Optimization

- Use Next.js font optimization
- Preload critical fonts
- Use font-display: swap
- Minimize font file sizes

## Caching Strategy

- Implement proper HTTP caching headers
- Use React Query for client-side caching
- Cache static assets
- Implement service worker for offline support

## Memory Management

- Clean up event listeners
- Avoid memory leaks in useEffect
- Properly dispose of subscriptions
- Use WeakMap/WeakSet when appropriate

## Network Optimization

- Minimize HTTP requests
- Use HTTP/2 or HTTP/3
- Implement request batching
- Use CDN for static assets

## Database Optimization (Future)

- Implement proper indexing
- Use connection pooling
- Optimize queries
- Implement caching layers

## Monitoring

- Track Core Web Vitals
- Monitor bundle size
- Track API response times
- Monitor error rates
- Use performance budgets

## Lazy Loading Patterns

```typescript
// Route-based code splitting
const TasksPage = lazy(() => import('@/pages/tasks'));

// Component-based code splitting
const HeavyComponent = lazy(() => import('./heavy-component'));

// Library-based code splitting
const loadChartLibrary = () => import('chart.js');
```

## Performance Monitoring

```typescript
// Track Core Web Vitals
export function reportWebVitals(metric: any) {
  if (metric.label === 'web-vital') {
    console.log(metric);
    // Send to analytics
  }
}

// Performance budget
const PERFORMANCE_BUDGET = {
  bundleSize: 250 * 1024, // 250KB
  lcp: 2500, // 2.5s
  fid: 100, // 100ms
  cls: 0.1,
};
```

